from the request's own reference (PoliciesController.cs:16-17), and the GET builds the body's reference from the route (PoliciesController.cs:21-22, 24-25). So the reference read back is just the route echoed back. The extra asserts at :28 and :52 repeat that echo. The lower-case test does not show that a case-insensitive lookup found the stored row, because the stub upper-cases the route itself (PoliciesController.cs:22). Reference_is_trimmed_and_upper_cased_in_the_Location_and_the_stored_policy (:33-40) has the same weakness. It is red today only because the DTO pattern at SellPolicyRequest.cs:22 rejects surrounding spaces before any trimming, so it gets a 400. Once green fixes that, an echoing stub would pass it too. Rule: 'The client supplies the reference. It is trimmed and upper-cased, then must match ^[A-Z0-9-]{3,20}$ … abc-1 and ABC-1 are the same policy.' Accepted means stored and readable as sold, and these tests never check that.</dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Files</dt><dd><a class="kit-file-line-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/blob/main/tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/SellReferenceTests.cs" aria-label="tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/SellReferenceTests.cs on GitHub" data-line="absent" data-comp="file-line-link · primitive · line absent"><span class="kit-file-line-link__text">tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/SellReferenceTests.cs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-file-line-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a> <a class="kit-file-line-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/blob/main/tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/Support/PoliciesClient.cs" aria-label="tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/Support/PoliciesClient.cs on GitHub" data-line="absent" data-comp="file-line-link · primitive · line absent"><span class="kit-file-line-link__text">tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/Support/PoliciesClient.cs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-file-line-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a> <a class="kit-file-line-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/blob/main/src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Controllers/PoliciesController.cs" aria-label="src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Controllers/PoliciesController.cs on GitHub" data-line="absent" data-comp="file-line-link · primitive · line absent"><span class="kit-file-line-link__text">src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Controllers/PoliciesController.cs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-file-line-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a> <a class="kit-file-line-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/blob/main/src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/SellPolicyRequest.cs" aria-label="src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/SellPolicyRequest.cs on GitHub" data-line="absent" data-comp="file-line-link · primitive · line absent"><span class="kit-file-line-link__text">src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/SellPolicyRequest.cs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-file-line-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a></dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Fix direction</dt><dd>every SELL-1 accept test, all five, must read back the values it sold, not only the reference. That means type, startDate, endDate, amount, autoRenew, the four property lines, the policyholders in order, the single term 1 and the single payment. At least one of those values must be one the canned body (PoliciesController.cs:24-30) and the builder defaults do not carry (see I3). For the lower-case test, read back those same distinctive values through the lower-case route, so only a lookup of the stored row can produce them. One shared read-back assertion that compares the policy to the request it sold would give this to every accept test. It should take the expected endDate as an explicit value from the test, not derive it. A test-side start.AddYears(1).AddDays(-1) gives 27 Feb 2029 for a 29 Feb 2028 start, while SELL-3 says 28 Feb. The same helper is the cause in I2.</dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Suggested test</dt><dd><span class="kit-finding-card__absent">not recorded in the excerpt</span></dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Fixed by</dt><dd><span class="kit-finding-card__fix"><span class="kit-sha-link__wrap" data-state="pop"><a class="kit-sha-link__sha kit-sha-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/commit/0fb16f8" aria-label="Commit 0fb16f8 on GitHub">0fb16f8<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-